  "KAFKA-17785": {
    "jira_id": "KAFKA-17785",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Kafka protocol documentation should include tagged field information",
    "description": "The Kafka documentation includes a description of the Kafka protocol ([https://kafka.apache.org/protocol]). This is useful to someone wanting to understand the details of the protocol. However, in the area of tagged fields, the documentation is not helpful.\r\n\r\nTagged fields provide a way of supplying optional data in a request or response. Modern requests and responses usually permit tagged fields, although they are relatively rarely used in practice.\r\n\r\nOne RPC in which tagged fields contain important information is the APIVersionsResponse. In v3 and above, the response contains the set of supported and finalised features, which can be used by a client to determine whether a broker supports a feature. This information is carried as tagged fields, but if you read the documentation of the protocol, you would be entirely in the dark.\r\n\r\nThis improvement adds tagged field information into the protocol documentation.",
